// Secrets.example.xcconfig — documents the keys the app expects for opt-in
// Supabase sync. Copy this file to Secrets.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in
// real values. NEVER commit Secrets.xcconfig and NEVER put the secret_key /
// service_role key anywhere in the app or repo — only the public publishable
// key ships.
//
// NOTE on xcconfig and "//": the sequence "//" starts a comment, so a URL like
// "https://example.supabase.co" would be truncated. Break the "//" with the
// $() expansion trick so the value survives: "https:/$()/example.supabase.co".
//
// SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is the public client key: the new publishable key
// "sb_publishable_..." (preferred). The legacy "anon" JWT still works in this
// slot until Supabase retires it (end of 2026). The secret key
// "sb_secret_..." / legacy service_role key must NEVER appear here.

SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/example.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY = sb_publishable_your-publishable-key-here
